Package: MycoHalo
Title: Colour-Calibrated Quantification of Fungal Melanization in Confrontation Assays
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Mitra", "Ghotbi", email = "mitra.ghotbi@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-9185-9993"))
Description: Image analysis of Petri-dish photographs for quantifying
    melanization of fungal colonies (developed for 'Zymoseptoria tritici')
    grown at fixed inoculation positions, alone or confronted with a
    bacterium. Pixels are analysed in the CIE 1976 L*a*b* colour space
    after flat-field illumination correction, so that grey fungal colonies,
    whitish bacterial colonies and yellowish diffusion halos, which overlap
    in grayscale, are separated by a layout-initialised Gaussian mixture of
    colour and texture. Individual colonies sharing one dish are separated
    by a marker-controlled watershed seeded at the known inoculation points.
    The package reports colony size and shape, melanization indices with
    spatial block-bootstrap confidence intervals, edge-to-centre profiles,
    side-specific (facing versus away from the bacterium) melanization,
    growth inhibition, halo geometry and quality-control figures, and
    provides a plate simulator with known ground truth for validation.
